course: dictionary
lesson: 826
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one is meant. Belly is a good example. It can mean the front of your body, your stomach, or the underside of an animal or a thing.
explain: «Picture an animal so tall that a giraffe could almost walk under its belly.» The words walk under tell you that belly means the underside of the animal, not a tummy. Ask yourself which meaning fits the sentence, then swap it in to check.
explain: Some words belong to phrases, and the phrase has its own meaning. A «belly laugh» is a big, deep laugh. It is not about a tummy at all. A «belly flop» is a painful, flat dive into water, and «a full belly» means someone has eaten well.
fact: Belly means the front part of the body, between the chest and the legs; it is another word for tummy.
fact: Belly can also mean the stomach, where food goes.
fact: Belly can mean the rounded underside of an animal, or of a thing such as a boat or a plane.
fact: «Belly laugh» means a big, deep laugh, and «belly flop» means a painful, flat dive.
fact: A good check is to swap your meaning into the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
exercise: «Ring-tailed lemurs sit in the morning sun, warming their bellies after a cold night.» What are the lemurs warming? | Their paws only | Their ears | *The front of their bodies, where the tummy is | Their tails
exercise: «Picture an animal so tall that a giraffe could almost walk under its belly.» What does belly mean here? | The food inside its stomach | *The underside of the animal | A big, deep laugh | A flat dive into water
exercise: Ben says a «belly laugh» is a laugh you do with your tummy. What does belly laugh really mean? | A quiet giggle behind a hand | A laugh you do after eating | *A big, deep laugh
test:
«In the small intestine, a tube about six metres long folded up in your belly, the food is broken down fully.» What does belly mean here? | A deep laugh | The underside of a boat | *The tummy, the front part of the body | A flat dive
test:
Ella reads that someone has «a full belly» after dinner. What does this phrase mean? | They are very tall | *They have eaten well | They are feeling sad | They are wearing a belt
exam:
«Male emperor penguins huddle in thousands, each with an egg on his feet under a warm fold of belly skin.» In this sentence, belly skin is the skin on the | *underside of the body | top of the head | back of the tail | wings only
